(3887064, 549538, 6999, '<td valign="top">As an illustrative image, as opposed to a found image, it seems OK to comment on the set-up; and I would wish there were more space around the broken glass - that the fragments were more distinguishable: they''re crammed into very little frame-space really. The concept is OK, and well executed otherwise.</td>', 'As an illustrative image, as opposed to a found image, it seems OK to comment on the set-up; and I would wish there were more space around the broken glass - that the fragments were more distinguishable: they''re crammed into very little frame-space really. The concept is OK, and well executed otherwise.', '2007-07-09 20:54:03.000000', NULL, 1),
(3887068, 551026, 6999, '<td valign="top">A little blatant, and the angularity seems forced, and removes a sense of connection between the two elements to my eye. Almost like a pastiche image, rather than a single unity. Decent studio execution, if a bit flat on the lighting.</td>', 'A little blatant, and the angularity seems forced, and removes a sense of connection between the two elements to my eye. Almost like a pastiche image, rather than a single unity. Decent studio execution, if a bit flat on the lighting.', '2007-07-09 20:56:04.000000', NULL, 1),
(3887080, 551130, 6999, '<td valign="top">I suspect your message may be a little obtuse for many - I hope I''m wrong. I like the parallels - the highs and lows of the wave of horizon framing the parallel points of the subjects; also like the reliance on the smallest possible details to carry the message - gives us some idea of a sense of futility in both these aspirations.</td>', 'I suspect your message may be a little obtuse for many - I hope I''m wrong. I like the parallels - the highs and lows of the wave of horizon framing the parallel points of the subjects; also like the reliance on the smallest possible details to carry the message - gives us some idea of a sense of futility in both these aspirations.', '2007-07-09 20:59:49.000000', NULL, 1),
