(6134782, 550886, 97270, '<td valign="top">Not a big fan of overused partial de-sat, but this one caught my attention. It does give an interesting perspective into the passing of life and how fragile it is. I would have preferred to see the kid''s shoes in Sepia, and they would still pop out. Another thing I would have tried differently is to see the scene from a lower angle.<br/> <br/><a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/forum.php?action=read&amp;FORUM_THREAD_ID=1025183" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">[The Comment or Die Thread - 2]</a> <br/></td>', 'Not a big fan of overused partial de-sat, but this one caught my attention. It does give an interesting perspective into the passing of life and how fragile it is. I would have preferred to see the kid''s shoes in Sepia, and they would still pop out. Another thing I would have tried differently is to see the scene from a lower angle. [The Comment or Die Thread - 2] ', '2010-08-18 22:41:22.000000', NULL, 0),
